  "verdict": "the_closing_commit_is_in_two_halves_the_added_member_moves_the_name_census_and_the_wiring_edit_moves_only_counts_so_the_two_readings_could_not_separate_them_and_excluding_the_family_leaves_most_of_these_names_with_no_writer_at_all",
  "reasons": [
    "every closer adds a census study and edits the wiring file in the same commit: 18 census studies and 16 wiring edits over 15 distinct commits",
    "the added member names its own face in 16/16 windows and names a stem that already had a writer in 8/16, so the corpus grows by a self-named measurement every time",
    "the wiring half moves 0 name(s) while editing 360 lines / 23863 bytes in place, so it is visible to every counting face and invisible to the name census -- that is why E338's two readings coincided",
    "excluding the family at the pin removes 0.7% of sources and 1.3% of lines and leaves 15 of 22 measured names with no writer at all"
  ],
  "limits": {
    "name_currency_is_a_proxy": "no census face is re-run at each closing commit -- the population those faces read is not reconstructible from an old tree alone.  The mover is measured in the family's own needle currency (stems named by a source), which is the composed step of E322's needle, not a published number",
    "pinned_commit": "the exclusion cost is read at 444d3be87; this study's own file lands after it, so the pinned corpus is one .py smaller than the tree that publishes this face",
    "self_disclosure": "this file is itself a new .py in the population every census face reads, so it closes windows the same way its siblings did"
  }
}
